<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Manuel III of Trebizond</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1364">1364</a>–<a href="/years/1417">1417</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Manuel III was Emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trabzon">Trebizond</a> from 1390 to 1417, the son of Alexios III. Faced with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timur">Timur</a>'s advance into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a>, he accepted Timur's overlordship, and after Timur defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ankara">Ankara</a> in 1402 Trebizond enjoyed a respite from Ottoman pressure. He was succeeded by his son Alexios IV.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/manuel-iii-of-trebizond.jpg" alt="Manuel III of Trebizond" width="320" height="269" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG Coins · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manuel_III_of_Trebizond_coin.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
